\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false. As a result, $C\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981514/state.json" "file_sha256" "8af456eb8a8c4c04b0b9d790ca8494c14313f22c7a03a2c04fb86c5945cd57cc"} {"question" "q-102666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c410cfe1cbce8ad8d3ea9b3510f6a3e7410b37a98890fcfb8401466d573874fc"} {"question" "q-102666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981514/state.json" "file_sha256" "8af456eb8a8c4c04b0b9d790ca8494c14313f22c7a03a2c04fb86c5945cd57cc"} {"question" "q-102666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I only"] [